Live on your management cluster: podinfo. Each variant's profile deploys the same add-ons to the same cluster, and Sveltos lets one profile manage a release at a time, so the per-cluster profiles wait until the live one steps aside. apply also writes takeover.sh, which hands each release over without reinstalling it; run it after apply.sh. See "If your profiles are live" in docs/user/onboard-your-sveltos-fleet.md.

Wrote onboard/apply.sh and the files it reads. Read it, then run it:
  MGMT_CONTEXT=<kubectl context of your management cluster> bash onboard/apply.sh

Then hand the live profiles over, without reinstalling anything:
  MGMT_CONTEXT=<same context> bash onboard/takeover.sh
apiVersion: config.projectsveltos.io/v1beta1
kind: ClusterProfile
metadata:
  name: podinfo-base
spec:
  clusterRefs: []
  continueOnConflict: false
  continueOnError: false
  helmCharts:
    - chartName: podinfo/podinfo
      chartVersion: 6.7.1
      helmChartAction: Install
      releaseName: podinfo
      releaseNamespace: podinfo
      repositoryName: podinfo
      repositoryURL: https://stefanprodan.github.io/podinfo
  reloader: false
  stopMatchingBehavior: WithdrawPolicies
  syncMode: ContinuousWithDriftDetection
  tier: 100

